  "data": {
    "body": "It is known that one of the solutions of the differential equation \n\n\\[\nx^2 y'' - x y' - 15y = 0 \\quad (x > 0)\n\\]\n\nis $y_1(x)=x^5$. Use the method of reduction of order to find a second linearly independent solution $y_2(x)$. Recall that this method consists of substituting $y_2(x) = v(x)y_1(x)$ into the differential equation above and reducing it to a first order equation for $v'$.",
    "solution": "$y_2=x^{-3}$",
